#
# The flagship acceptance manifest — the language grounding layer's depth bar as a typed contract.
#
# The language grounding layer's depth is defined by five flagship acceptance scenarios,
# not by adjectives. Each is realized by a worked example, pinned by a competency
# question, emitted by a named native producer, and guarded by a counter-example that
# raises a named failure class. This manifest reifies the acceptance bar ITSELF: five
# gmeow:FlagshipScenario individuals, each binding one scenario to the artifacts that
# realize and enforce it —
#   gmeow:demonstratedByExample     -> the worked example fixture
#   gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency  -> the gmeow:CompetencyQuestion that pins it
#   gmeow:demonstratedByProducer    -> the native entrypoint the production DAG owns
#   gmeow:guardedByCounterExample   -> the minimal violation that proves the gate bites
#   gmeow:enforcesFailureClass      -> the lang:LangConformanceFailure subclass it raises
#
# The bindings are gated across three surfaces. SHACL (lang:FlagshipScenarioShape) and a
# structural ASK (ex:saFlagshipCoverage) check the five are present and fully linked with
# a real failure class. The native flagship cross-check resolves each
# gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency into tests/competency.ttl and confirms it carries a
# gmeow:cqExpectRow expectation and an existing query file (the competency-question
# individuals live in the tests dataset, which SHACL never loads — hence the split). The
# authenticated slice-spec producer executes the competency and conformance cells once,
# while the named language producers run in the production DAG and publish cached stage
# receipts. Tests consume those receipts and never rebuild either corpus. Validates cleanly.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix lang: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/lang/> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix exa:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/lang/acceptance/> .
@prefix cq:   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/lang/tests/> .

# --- Flagship 1 — a sentence to a formula, compositionally ----------------- #
exa:sentenceToFormula a gmeow:FlagshipScenario ;
    rdfs:label "Flagship: a sentence to a formula, compositionally"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The declarative sentence \"cats chase mice\" denotes a full-FOL logic:Formula through a compositional lowering (form AST -> Montagovian composition -> logic: FOL), each step carrying a logic:preservationKind, pinned by the denotes-to-formula competency and produced by the native lang-bridge SVO lowering."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByExample "tests/conformance-fixtures/meaning-cats-chase-mice.ttl" ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency cq:cqDenotationsToFormula ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByProducer "pipeline::stages::lang_lowering::build_corpus" ;
    gmeow:guardedByCounterExample "tests/counter-examples/meaning-underspecified-denotation.ttl" ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass lang:UnderspecifiedDenotation ;
    skos:note "Structural discharge is irreducible here: the guard omits a required denotation field, and open-world reasoning cannot infer that a value does not exist. The class-scoped closed-world validation projection is the authoritative executable negative."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:counterExampleDischarge gmeow:structuralDischarge .

# --- Flagship 2 — GMEOW reading its own prose ------------------------------ #
exa:proseSelfReading a gmeow:FlagshipScenario ;
    rdfs:label "Flagship: GMEOW reading its own prose"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Every @x-gmeow-english source literal is lifted to a content-addressed lang:SurfaceForm carrying its prose-hash (logic:candidateSourceHash) and an exact surface round-trip logic:Correspondence — dogfooding. The shape is pinned by the prose-lift competency; the totality (every literal) is discharged by executing the lang_form prose-lift stage over the real slice catalog."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByExample "tests/conformance-fixtures/meaning-prose-lift-hashed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency cq:cqProseLiftHashed ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByProducer "pipeline::stages::lang_form::build_corpus" ;
    gmeow:guardedByCounterExample "tests/counter-examples/surface-unhashable.ttl" ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass lang:UnhashableSurface ;
    skos:note "Structural discharge is irreducible here: the guard omits material-identity fields, and their absence is a closed-world validation fact rather than a DL contradiction. The producer separately proves corpus-wide lift totality."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:counterExampleDischarge gmeow:structuralDischarge .

# --- Flagship 3 — the multilingual docs trees as translation --------------- #
exa:docsAsTranslation a gmeow:FlagshipScenario ;
    rdfs:label "Flagship: the multilingual docs trees as translation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The multilingual docs catalogs are lang:TranslationUnits, each crossing carrying its adequacy on a logic:Correspondence rather than a silent Exact default — the per-unit preservation judgment in the loss ledger. Pinned by the projection-loss-against-canon competency and produced by the native lang_translation stage over the real .po catalogs."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByExample "tests/conformance-fixtures/translation-french-english-pair.ttl" ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency cq:cqProjectionLossAgainstCanon ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByProducer "pipeline::stages::lang_translation::build_corpus" ;
    gmeow:guardedByCounterExample "tests/counter-examples/translation-unit-underspecified.ttl" ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass lang:UnderspecifiedTranslationUnit ;
    skos:note "Structural discharge is irreducible here: a missing source, target, or correspondence is observable only under the unit's declared closed-world validation contract; an open-world reasoner may not conclude absence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:counterExampleDischarge gmeow:structuralDischarge .

# --- Flagship 4 — GMEOW's serializations as grammars ----------------------- #
exa:serializationsAsGrammars a gmeow:FlagshipScenario ;
    rdfs:label "Flagship: GMEOW's serializations as grammars"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "GMEOW's Turtle/GTS/GMN serialization grammars are lang:Grammar objects; parse is interpretation and emit is rendering, and the emit/parse round-trip is exact (a lossless crossing carrying logic:ExactPreservation). Pinned by the grammar-round-trip competency and produced by the native lang_projection stage lifting the real grammars/*.ebnf into the bundle."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByExample "tests/conformance-fixtures/rendering-turtle-emit.ttl" ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency cq:cqGrammarRoundTrip ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByProducer "pipeline::stages::lang_projection::build_corpus" ;
    gmeow:guardedByCounterExample "tests/counter-examples/projection-exact-preservation-violated.ttl" ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass lang:ExactPreservationViolated ;
    skos:note "Structural discharge is irreducible here: exact round-trip failure is established by executing the serializer/parser section-retraction path over artifacts, not by a static DL entailment over the manifest."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:counterExampleDischarge gmeow:structuralDischarge .

# --- Flagship 5 — ambiguity held honestly ---------------------------------- #
exa:ambiguityHeldHonestly a gmeow:FlagshipScenario ;
    rdfs:label "Flagship: ambiguity held honestly"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An ambiguous form keeps every reading as first-class co-resident data with its vantage; a projection emits one artifact per reading and never silently collapses to one, and an unrouted ambiguous denotation is rejected. Pinned by the co-resident-readings competency and produced by the native lang_projection stage."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByExample "tests/conformance-fixtures/meaning-scope-ambiguity.ttl" ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency cq:cqCoresidentReadings ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByProducer "pipeline::stages::lang_projection::build_corpus" ;
    gmeow:guardedByCounterExample "tests/counter-examples/meaning-unrouted-ambiguous.ttl" ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass lang:UnroutedAmbiguousDenotation ;
    skos:note "Structural discharge is irreducible here: the failure joins a data-dependent multiplicity of recorded senses with the absence of lang:viaSense, a closed-world guarded-existence check that OWL cannot prove from omission."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:counterExampleDischarge gmeow:structuralDischarge .
